            <ArticleTitle>Sudden cardiac death associated with Churg-Strauss syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2355-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 60-year-old man who had serious chest and arm pain died suddenly during hospitalization. He suffered from coronary vasospastic angina complicated by a fatal acute fulminant-type of myocarditis associated with Churg-Strauss syndrome (CSS). The diagnosis at autopsy was acute progressive eosinophilic myocarditis associated with CSS.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
